{"text": "Human development is now increasingly understood as an ongoing, flexible, and evolving process rather than a fixed sequence of stages. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At the core of this perspective lies the concept of plasticity. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Plasticity refers to the human capacity to change, adapt, and reorganize cognitive, emotional, and behavioural patterns in response to life experiences, environmental demands, and biological changes. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It highlights that individuals are not merely passive recipients of development but active agents capable of growth throughout their lives. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In earlier views, development was believed to occur mainly during childhood, with adulthood seen as a period of stability and old age as a phase of decline. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The concept of plasticity challenges this rigid outlook by emphasizing that development continues across the entire lifespan. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Although the extent of change may vary at different stages, every phase of life allows room for adaptation and transformation.", "alignment": {"characters": ["H", "u", "m", "a", "n", " ", "d", "e", "v", "e", "l", "o", "p", "m", "e", "n", "t", " ", "i", "s", " ", "n", "o", "w", " ", "i", "n", "c", "r", "e", "a", "s", "i", "n", "g", "l", "y", " ", "u", "n", "d", "e", "r", "s", "t", "o", "o", "d", " ", "a", "s", " ", "a", "n", " ", "o", "n", "g", "o", "i", "n", "g", ",", " ", "f", "l", "e", "x", "i", "b", "l", "e", ",", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "e", "v", "o", "l", "v", "i", "n", "g", " ", "p", "r", "o", "c", "e", "s", "s", " ", "r", "a", "t", "h", "e", "r", " ", "t", "h", "a", "n", " ", "a", " ", "f", "i", "x", "e", "d", " ", "s", "e", "q", "u", "e", "n", "c", "e", " ", "o", "f", " ", "s", "t", "a", "g", "e", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "A", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "c", "o", "r", "e", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t",